{"tool_name":"heca","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"heca","home":"http://eca.xglab.tech/","license":"Not licensed","summary":"The human Ensemble Cell Atlas (hECA) a database.","addition_date":"2022-08-26T08:56:24.116437Z","last_update_date":"2022-08-26T08:56:24.120240Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:heca","credit":[{"email":"zhangxg@tsinghua.edu.cn","name":"Xuegong Zhang","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"}]}],"name":"hECA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/J.ISCI.2022.104318","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022 The Author(s)The accumulation of massive single-cell omics data provides growing resources for building biomolecular atlases of all cells of human organs or the whole body. The true assembly of a cell atlas should be cell-centric rather than file-centric. We developed a unified informatics framework for seamless cell-centric data assembly and built the human Ensemble Cell Atlas (hECA) from scattered data. hECA v1.0 assembled 1,093,299 labeled human cells from 116 published datasets, covering 38 organs and 11 systems. We invented three new methods of atlas applications based on the cell-centric assembly: \u201cin data\u201d cell sorting for targeted data retrieval with customizable logic expressions, \u201cquantitative portraiture\u201d for multi-view representations of biological entities, and customizable reference creation for generating references for automatic annotations. Case studies on agile construction of user-defined sub-atlases and \u201cin data\u201d investigation of CAR-T off-targets in multiple organs showed the great potential enabled by the cell-centric ensemble atlas.","authors":[{"name":"Bian H."},{"name":"Chen F."},{"name":"Chen S."},{"name":"Chen Y."},{"name":"Cui Y."},{"name":"Gao H."},{"name":"Hao M."},{"name":"Hua K."},{"name":"Jiang R."},{"name":"Li C."},{"name":"Li F."},{"name":"Li H."},{"name":"Li J."},{"name":"Li W."},{"name":"Li W."},{"name":"Luo Y."},{"name":"Lv H."},{"name":"Meng Q."},{"name":"Wang X."},{"name":"Wei L."},{"name":"Xi X."},{"name":"Ye M."},{"name":"You R."},{"name":"Zhang X."},{"name":"Zhang Y."},{"name":"Zou Z."}],"date":"2022-05-20T00:00:00Z","journal":"iScience","title":"hECA: The cell-centric assembly of a cell atlas"},"pmcid":"PMC9114628","pmid":"35602947"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Human biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2815"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Regenerative medicine","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3395"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"hECA","home":"https://bio.tools/heca","license":"Not licensed","summary":"The human Ensemble Cell Atlas (hECA) a database.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:heca/db/eca.xglab.tech","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":26,"citations":[{"count":3,"year":"2022"},{"count":4,"year":"2023"},{"count":4,"year":"2024"},{"count":4,"year":"2026"},{"count":11,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1016/j.isci.2022.104318","pmcid":"PMC9114628","pmid":"3560294